      "text": [
        " اَلْبِئْرِ قَدْ تَفَسَّخَ فَقَالَ «إِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ أَنْ تَنْزَحَ مِنْهَا سَبْعَةَ دِلاَءٍ فَقَالَ لَهُ فَثِيَابُنَا قَدْ صَلَّيْنَا فِيهَا نَغْسِلُهَا وَ نُعِيدُ اَلصَّلاَةَ قَالَ لاَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.32 - Yaqub ibn Uthaym asked Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) about a gecko that was found decayed in a well.\nImam (as) said: \"You only need to draw seven buckets from it.\"\nYa'qub then asked: \"Our clothes that we prayed in—do we need to wash them and repeat the prayer?\"\nImam (as) said: \"No.\""
        ]
      }
